s a known potent  irreversible neurotoxin it impacts  cognition IQ levels behavior we now know  based on incredible science there is no  safe level of lead exposure at all yeah  and in a small part - but so many people  knew about this Mona that's the thing  when you raise the flag your call  irresponsible unfortunate researcher  causing near hysteria splicing and  dicing  the numbers yeah so lots of folks knew  about this crisis there was many many  red flags just a few months after we  switched this water source General  Motors which was born in Flint stopped  using this water because it was  corroding engine parts so imagine that  corroding engine parts what's it doing  to our plumbing what was it like to go  through that period where your drum  being discredited in public in American  life right now there are a lot of people  who are who are not speaking up are  trying to speak up and there are big  forces against them so what was it like  being inside of that for yes it was it  was hard it was traumatic my heart rate  went up my might I was shaking I just  wanted to hide under the covers for a  moment but but then I realized that it's  it's my professional professional my  morale my ethical obligation to speak up  for these kids I'm a pediatrician I  literally took an oath to protect  children to be their healer to make sure  that they're not only healthy today but  that they're healthy forever so you know  I all my research was based on numbers  and statistics but every number was a  kid a kid who who I probably took care  of and and that's what inspired me to  speak up in that piece we saw people  still have concerns about the water in  Flint should they absolutely  this isn't as a loss of trust in Flint  for for so long they were betrayed by  really every government agency that was  that was meant to protect them would you  drink the water there I now knowing  about kind of federal standards about  letting water  I don't drink unfiltered water anywhere  our 